cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below. If you cite a measured figure, cite the commit and the split it came from."
title: "Project FLAME: Fixed-step orchestrator for accelerated play — integer timebase, no dropped ticks."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: CDDL-1.1
type: software
abstract: >-
  FLAME is a fixed-step game engine orchestrator with an integer timebase
  that guarantees no dropped ticks. It runs on the Python standard library
  with no runtime dependencies. The engine provides deterministic simulation
  suitable for accelerated play, testing, and replay.
authors:
  - name: "Project FLAME contributors"
keywords:
  - game engine
  - fixed-step
  - integer timebase
  - deterministic simulation
  - open source
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Godot Engine"
    notes: "Reference for open-source game engine architecture."
    url: "https://godotengine.org/"